        <mxCell id="legend" value="&lt;b&gt;Legend&lt;/b&gt;&#xa;&#x25A0; gray = HumanMessage      &#x25A0; purple = AIMessage      &#x25A0; red border = NEW this turn      &#x25A0; blue dashed = your app's storage" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#cccccc;fontSize=11;align=left;verticalAlign=middle;spacing=10;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="40" y="780" width="1620" height="50" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="caption" value="&lt;b&gt;What this shows.&lt;/b&gt;  The model never &quot;remembers&quot; anything. It is the same stateless function called three times. The reason it appears to remember is that on Turn 2 your app re-sent Turn 1, and on Turn 3 your app re-sent Turns 1 and 2. The history lives in your application&#x2019;s message list, not in the model.&#xa;&#xa;&lt;b&gt;Cost consequence.&lt;/b&gt;  Turn 1 sent 1 message worth of tokens. Turn 3 sent 5 messages worth. Turn 100 sends 100+ messages worth. Linear-in-N tokens, every single turn. Diagram 3 shows the wall this leads to." style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#fff2cc;strokeColor=#d6b656;fontSize=12;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacing=14;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="40" y="850" width="1620" height="160" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>

